  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "reading वातुलः for चाटुलः avoids repetition, the meaning in that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "case being ‘delirious’; but when we look to what the common",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "parlance is in this connection, this reading does not seem to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "be preferable.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 59. उद्भा०—of one that has brightened all wicked men,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "i. e. a scoundrel of the first rank, who has brought credit to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "whole class. विशृंखल—unbridled; one licensed as it were to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "indulge in all sorts of wicked deeds. प्राग्जाता &c.—see com.; It",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "will be inappropriate to analyse as कर्मसु वृत्तिः since it continues",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "even now. With the reading विस्तृत for विस्मृत the sense is–‘whose",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "indulgence in wicked conduct commenced before is now",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "developed.’–Telang. In this case dissolve प्राग्जाता पश्चात् विस्तृता",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "निजाधमकर्मसु वृत्तिः यस्य ।",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 60. This verse very cleverly describes friendship as we",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "find it in the world. Insincere friendship shows at its high-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "est at the very beginning, but gradually vanishes and is com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "pared to the shadow in the morning which is longest at sun-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "rise and goes on contracting till noon. A good man’s friend-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "ship, however, is hardly preceptible, like the mid-day shadow,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "at first, but goes on steadily increasing.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "गुर्वी—Fem. of गुरु; also गुरु; see notes on Sl. 20. दिनस्य—to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "connected with पूर्वार्ध &c. by what is called एकदेशी अन्वय like",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "देवदत्तस्य गुरुकुलम् ; see note on परेषां Sl. 20. The fig. is उपमा mixed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "with यथासंख्य.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 61. तृणः—&c.–निष्कारण–those that are causelessly enemies;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "निष्कारणं वैरिणः । The fig. of speech here is यथासंख्य which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "is defined as यथासंख्यं क्रमेणैव क्रमिकाणां समन्वयः K. P. X. Here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "लुब्धक, धीवर and पिशुन are mentioned as the respective enemies",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of मृग, मीन and सज्जन.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 62. व्यसनं—close application, strong attachment. खले",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "संसर्गमुक्तिः—There is एकदेशी अन्वय here, खले यः संसर्गः तस्मात्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "मुक्तिः । We have preferred the sing. to the plural as it keeps up",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
